        "answer": {
          "short": "$(30+12\\pi)\\,\\mathrm{m}^{2}$",
          "worked": "Add the two quarter-circle ends, the quarter-cylinder curved surface and both rectangular cut faces.\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac12\\pi r^{2}+\\frac12\\pi rh+2rh\\\\A&=\\frac12\\pi(3)^{2}+\\frac12\\pi(3)(5)+2(3)(5)\\\\A&=\\frac{9\\pi}{2}+\\frac{15\\pi}{2}+30\\\\A&=(30+12\\pi)\\,\\mathrm{m}^{2}\\end{align*}$$",
